# Line-ending policy.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to
# CRLF on checkout. That is harmless for most files and fatal for anything Linux
# executes: a shell script with CRLF endings makes the kernel read the shebang as
# "/bin/sh\r", and the container fails with "no such file or directory" naming a
# script that is visibly present. Force LF on everything the image runs or builds.
#
# THIS is what keeps entrypoint.sh from being checked out with CRLF and failing 
inside the container with a baffling no such file or directory.

* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf

# Binary-ish artifacts that must never be line-ending translated.
*.gguf      binary
*.safetensors binary
*.png       binary
*.pdf       binary
